  <div class="card"><h2>1) Student Demographic Overview</h2><div class="two"><div id="gender"></div><div id="district_count"></div></div><div class="two"><div id="age_hist"></div><div id="school_type"></div></div></div>

  <div class="card"><h2>2) Academic Performance Analysis</h2><div class="two"><div id="gpa_dist"></div><div id="perf_band"></div></div><p><span class="badge">Pass Rate (HSC ≥ 2.0): {pass_rate:.1f}%</span> The average progression from previous GPA to HSC is <b>{kpis['gpa_delta']:+.2f}</b>, indicating {'overall improvement' if kpis['gpa_delta']>=0 else 'overall decline'}.</p></div>

  <div class="card"><h2>3) Socio-Economic Factors and Their Impact on Performance</h2>
    <p><b>Most critical finding:</b> Socio-economic status aligns strongly with HSC outcomes. Students in the highest income quartile outperform those in the lowest quartile by <b>{income_gap:.2f}</b> GPA points on average. Internet access is associated with a <b>{internet_gap:.2f}</b> GPA advantage, and parent education level spans a <b>{parent_gap:.2f}</b> GPA gap between lowest and highest groups.</p>
